{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1334062-fallen-london","id":1334062,"title":"Fallen London","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-05T04:19:39-07:00","id":1334062,"title":"Fallen London","content":"So, I've got a Mage/Demon crossover game coming up, and I think I'm going to be setting it in London. I've got a fair amount of good stuff from the London entry in Mage 2e, and more I can crib and alter from other games (Fantasy Flight's <i>Fireborn</i> comes to mind), but I'm a little short of material to use on the Demon side of things.<br /> <br /> One idea I had was that the Machine in London is basically experimenting with the 'runewalks', trying to incorporate them into its Infrastructure. This, of course, raises the terrifying possibility of the Machine - or at least some fraction thereof - getting insight into the Supernal and, potentially, even Awakening (or something like that process). Whether or not that's actually <i>possible</i> honestly matters less than the fact that the PCs could think it is.<br /> <br /> So, anyone got any ideas that could be used here, particularly for Infrastructure, angels or G-M cults? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24502\" data-vbnamecard=\"24502\">KieranMullen</a> had some great stuff for linking demons and mages in the plot hooks thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"